 "updated_at": 1790305434.557524, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "sibling_fields_used": [], "sibling_field_chars": {}, "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 1, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "5f30a4e6-40d2-4006-a73b-3bff1baa48cf", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790305435.693619, "updated_at": 1790305435.693619, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "sibling_fields_used": [], "sibling_field_chars": {}, "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "aefc76c5-94c8-47aa-a2bd-f7c5f5069d06", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790305435.700167, "updated_at": 1790305435.700167, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "sibling_fields_used": ["content"], "sibling_field_chars": {"content": 13}, "text": "Worked for 5s", "text_chars": 13, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "7d976b69-2d4f-4821-b608-72a2114b5f01", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790305435.704776, "updated_at": 1790305450.601281, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "sibling_fields_used": [], "sibling_field_chars": {}, "text": "Yeah — if you mean **cash-advance / paycheck-advance apps like EarnIn and Brigit**, there are quite a few legitimate ones now.\n\nThe main ones I’d look at are **Dave, MoneyLion Instacash, Klover, Cleo, Current, Chime MyPay/SpotMe, Albert, and Tilt** (formerly Empower). NerdWallet’s current 2026 comparison includes Brigit, Current, Dave, EarnIn, Klover, MoneyLion, and Tilt among the major options. citeturn303536search13\n\nA few stand out depending on what you’re trying to do:\n\n- **MoneyLion Instacash** — potentially up to about **$500**, no mandatory monthly subscription for standard delivery; instant/expedited delivery can cost extra. citeturn303536search1\n- **Dave ExtraCash** — one of the bigger mainstream competitors and tends to be geared toward quick advances.\n- **Klover** — usually smaller advances but can be useful as another independent source.\n- **Cleo** — advances generally **$20–$250** on Plus/Pro, with larger amounts possible under Builder; standard delivery is free, while same-day delivery currently runs roughly **$4.49–$14.99**. citeturn303536search4turn303536search5\n- **Current** — worth checking especially if you already use or are willing to use their banking product.\n- **Chime** — SpotMe/MyPay can serve essentially the same purpose if you meet their direct-deposit/account requirements.\n- **Tilt** — formerly Empower; currently advertises cash advances up to around **$500**, though there's an **$8/month** subscription after the trial. citeturn303536search6\n- **Albert** — another large player, though I'd pay attention to the subscription structure before signing up.\n\nFor **your situation**, where the objective sounds like *“I need an extra $50–$300 bridge and I want to know what can actually fund me now,”* I'd probably test them in this order: **MoneyLion → Dave → Klover → Cleo → Current/Chime**, rather than signing up for five monthly subscriptions at once.\n\nOne important thing: approval amounts are **very account-specific**. Two apps advertising $500 can give one person $25 and another person $300 based on recurring deposits, checking-account history, balance patterns, and prior repayment behavior. citeturn303536search13\n\nIf you tell me **roughly how much you're trying to bridge — like $50, $100, $200, or $500 — and whether you have direct deposit**, I can narrow it down to the **2–3 most realistic ones to try tonight**.", "text_chars": 2392, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}], "ordering_is_monotonic": true, "total_text_chars": 2491, "code_block_count": 0, "link_count": 0, "citation_count": 0, "path_reference_count": 0, "model_slugs": ["gpt-5-6-thinking"], "unextractable_part_kinds": [], "capture": {"capture_status": "ok", "captured_at": "2026-09-26T08:38:48Z", "capture_path": null, "pages_walked": 1, "content_types": ["model_editable_context", "reasoning_recap", "text", "thoughts"], "warnings": []}, "provenance": {"observation_id": "4f5b62839ba748788e9362493d39ac64", "source_artifact_path": "C:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother\\Projects\\ACTIVE\\gce-ingestion-w1\\store\\chatgpt-backup\\EVIDENCE\\blobs\\sha256\\2f\\2f5cba336399f0d0e587a20cee16e0fc3f55deb08162d9e9db36b507f79c71f6", "source_content_hash": "2f5cba336399f0d0e587a20cee16e0fc3f55deb08162d9e9db36b507f79c71f6", "source_capture_timestamp": "2026-09-26T08:38:48.631782+00:00", "completeness_status": "COMPLETE", "normalizer_version": "gce.chatgpt.normalized.v1"}}